{"full":"hf:autotrust/JEV-27B-Demo","spaceId":"autotrust/JEV-27B-Demo","name":"JEV-27B Live Demo","source":"huggingface","description":"Play Mario, Rubik's Cube and Tetris with JEV-27B","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","decision-making","games","vizdoom","autotrust","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":93,"created":"2026-09-26T17:10:14.000Z","updated":"2026-09-30T16:55:54.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://autotrust-jev-27b-demo.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/autotrust/JEV-27B-Demo","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:31:31.352Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:31:31.352Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:31:31.352Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🎮","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Launch a live JEV-27B game run in the game arena.","The game worker runs on AutoTrust's existing B300 deployment. Model inputs are structured observations from the game engines. The display label is jev-27b-vl; the inference checkpoint is autotrust/JEV-27B. Cube actions use a fixed library of standard algorithms. Cube turns are animated independently of model inference timing. All raw run traces and rendered game frames are retained on the B300. The Space contains no Mario ROM.","The decision lab and Doom arena and demo reel remain available."],"features":["Mario: original NES World 1-1, with movement and jump decisions.","3D Rubik's Cube: a 25-turn scramble; select a seed or create a new scramble.","Tetris: smooth gravity acceleration, continuing at maximum speed until 20 lines.","The right panel shows the selected action, option probabilities, and current / average individual model inference duration. Mario movement and jump are separate calls.","Start and stop runs yourself; one run per game executes at a time, with a short queue. Recent runs reconnect when you reload the page."],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/autotrust/JEV-27B-Demo/blob/